; M4 gate: fm6 as an FM channel, in a score with no PCM (driver.md §14, D6).
; A score that uses PCM owns fm6 as the DAC for the whole song ($2B once, never
; given back) — mixing the two is E_FM6_DAC. So the gate for fm6-as-FM is a
; score WITHOUT PCM, and what it locks is the negative: $2B is never written,
; and fm6 keys on and off like any other channel.
(fm1 :tempo 120 :oct 4 :len 4 :vel 15   c   _   c   _)
(fm6 :oct 4 :len 4 :vel 15               _   e   _   e)
